From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] emulator: accept AT+BAC with CVSD anywhere in the list

Port Sailfish OS oFono 4208b6d9 ("[bluetooth] Be less pedantic about
ordering of speech codecs. Fixes JB#55276", Juho Hämäläinen).

bac_cb answers ERROR unless CVSD is the first codec in AT+BAC, and the
service level connection then fails. Some headsets list mSBC first.
CVSD is mandatory, so accept the list if it has CVSD anywhere and
reject it only if CVSD is missing. Sailfish also accepts a list without
CVSD; this keeps that one an error.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/src/emulator.c b/src/emulator.c
index 24e3451..2eb2d39 100644
--- a/src/emulator.c
+++ b/src/emulator.c
@@ -1009,6 +1009,8 @@ static void bac_cb(GAtServer *server, GAtServerRequestType type,
 {
 	struct ofono_emulator *em = user_data;
 	GAtResultIter iter;
+	bool cvsd = false;
+	bool msbc = false;
 	int val;
 
 	DBG("");
@@ -1021,22 +1023,17 @@ static void bac_cb(GAtServer *server, GAtServerRequestType type,
 			goto fail;
 
 		/*
-		 * CVSD codec is mandatory and must come first.
-		 * See HFP v1.6 4.34.1
+		 * CVSD codec is mandatory, and HFP v1.6 4.34.1 has it listed
+		 * first. Some headsets list mSBC first and otherwise work, so
+		 * only insist that CVSD is there.
 		 */
-		if (g_at_result_iter_next_number(&iter, &val) == FALSE ||
-				val != HFP_CODEC_CVSD)
-			goto fail;
-
-		em->bac_received = TRUE;
-
-		em->negotiated_codec = 0;
-		em->r_codecs[CVSD_OFFSET].supported = TRUE;
-
 		while (g_at_result_iter_next_number(&iter, &val)) {
 			switch (val) {
+			case HFP_CODEC_CVSD:
+				cvsd = true;
+				break;
 			case HFP_CODEC_MSBC:
-				em->r_codecs[MSBC_OFFSET].supported = TRUE;
+				msbc = true;
 				break;
 			default:
 				DBG("Unsupported HFP codec %d", val);
@@ -1044,6 +1041,17 @@ static void bac_cb(GAtServer *server, GAtServerRequestType type,
 			}
 		}
 
+		if (!cvsd)
+			goto fail;
+
+		em->bac_received = TRUE;
+
+		em->negotiated_codec = 0;
+		em->r_codecs[CVSD_OFFSET].supported = TRUE;
+
+		if (msbc)
+			em->r_codecs[MSBC_OFFSET].supported = TRUE;
+
 		g_at_server_send_final(server, G_AT_SERVER_RESULT_OK);
 
 		/*
